From 7154d8e5f519166415b25509c887e5994d18428f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:38:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] updates: the update channel of LibreELEC Hades in use

From 1.2 the image carries the update channel of LibreELEC Hades (the
package hades-update-channel), so the client of LibreELEC-settings-9016
is used. What it needed for that:

- a manifest has exactly the fields of its format: one missing, one more
  or one twice (in the manifest, its release, its file or the signature
  file), or NaN: it is not taken, and the log names the field;
- each release names the oldest release that it can be installed over
  (min_serial). A system older than that is not offered the download:
  "Available Versions" says that the version has to be installed with
  the installer or the files of its release, and "auto" never downloads
  it;
- a release without a manifest (the server answers 404) is a channel
  with nothing newer in it: no error, in the log or on the screen, and
  "Available Versions" says that this is the newest version. A manifest
  without its signature is still an error;
- a channel that could not be asked yet is asked again in ten minutes,
  not six hours: at a start whose clock is not set over the network yet,
  with no network yet, or with a video playing when it was to be asked.
  That is information in the log, not an error;
- with "manual" and the notifications off, the service does not ask the
  channel at all; "Available Versions" still does when it is chosen;
- the notifications name the version ("LibreELEC Hades 1.2.1"), say where
  to install it (Settings > LibreELEC > Updates) or that it waits for the
  next start, carry the mark of LibreELEC Hades (the icon of the program;
  the add-on's is LibreELEC's) and are not cut at 64 characters; the
  question before the download says that the system restarts to install
  it, and its progress bar is headed LibreELEC Hades; the help of
  "Automatic updates" is written anew: what "manual" and "auto" do, that
  only versions signed by LibreELEC Hades are taken and that looking sends
  nothing about the system, in three lines that fit its box (the text of
  1.0 with one sentence more was cut, seen on the screen). In English and
  the three Spanish of Hades (33190-33193, 32983).

And what a review of the client as an adversary found, before any system
used it:

- a redirect was followed to any HTTPS address, up to Python's ten. Now
  only to the same host and port or to one of the hosts that GitHub
  serves the files of a release from (github.com,
  release-assets.githubusercontent.com, objects.githubusercontent.com, on
  port 443), without a user in the address, four in a row at most; anything
  else is refused before it is asked. GitHub's chain today is two
  redirects: the newest release on github.com, then
  release-assets.githubusercontent.com;
- a proxy in the environment (https_proxy) was used: the request now goes
  to the address itself;
- a manifest that came a byte at a time held the service for as long as
  the server wanted (each read had its 30 seconds, and read() waits for
  all of it): it now has to come whole within 60 seconds, read as it
  comes. A download that brings less than 64 KiB in two minutes is given
  up, for the same reason;
- the room checked before a download was the file and 64 MiB; the init
  unpacks the file next to itself at the next start, so it is now twice
  the file and 128 MiB (with the copy of the kernel that a start with
  Secure Boot signs);
- the part file of a download cut short by a power cut or a kill of Kodi
  stayed in Kodi's temporary folder until the next download: it is removed
  when the add-on starts, never while a download runs;
- "auto" downloaded the same release again after a restart of Kodi before
  the system restarted: a file of that name in the update folder, whole
  and with the signed SHA-256, is now taken as downloaded;
- a manifest of 64 KiB of nested arrays, signed, made Python's JSON reader
  raise RecursionError, which nothing caught: it is now a manifest that is
  not valid, as is a state file that deep;
- the log no longer shows the query of an address (GitHub's addresses of
  files carry a signed one).

"Update Channel" with nothing to choose is hidden by hades_hide_unused of
LibreELEC-settings-9033, so the separate function of the first version of
this change is not needed.

Tested inside the system of the image of 1.1 (its Python, pycryptodome and
OpenSSL) against HTTPS servers that answer as GitHub does, with test keys
whose private halves are public: 264 checks. 27 of them fail on the client
before the review, and the test fails on each of 68 changes that take out
one of these protections or behaviours. In a virtual machine, a system of
this change with the channel took a newer one from a test server that
stands for GitHub, after its question, and its start installed it.
